@startuml wallet-data
' Render with: plantuml -tpng docs/Design/SoftArchitecture/figures/wallet-data.puml
!include style.iuml
set separator none
title Wallet module: its records, errors and tables

package "types.py" {
  class BalanceChangeReason <<public>> {
    + ACTIVITY_REWARD = "activity_reward"
    + TRADE_PURCHASE = "trade_purchase"
  }
  class LockedPortfolio <<public>> {
    + portfolio_id: UUID
    + user_id: UUID
  }
  class BalanceChangeReceipt <<public>> {
    + balance_change_id: UUID
    + amount: Decimal
    + cash_balance_after: Decimal
  }
  class InsufficientFundsError <<error>> {
    + code = "insufficient_funds"
    + status = 409
  }
}

package "routes.py" {
  class Balance <<data>> {
    + cash_balance: Money
  }
}

package "models.py" {
  class "Portfolio (portfolios)" as Portfolio <<table>> {
    + portfolio_id: UUID
    + user_id: UUID
    + cash_balance: Decimal
    + scenario_id: UUID or None
    + created_at: datetime
    .. the database refuses ..
    cash_balance < 0, or NaN
    a second live portfolio for a user
    a user_id with no user
  }
  class "BalanceChange (balance_changes)" as BalanceChange <<table>> {
    + balance_change_id: UUID
    + portfolio_id: UUID
    + amount: Decimal
    + reason: str
    + activity_date: date or None
    + created_at: datetime
    .. the database refuses ..
    amount = 0, or NaN
    a reason that isn't a BalanceChangeReason
    a reward that spends, a purchase that adds
    a reward with no activity_date
    anything else with an activity_date
    a portfolio_id with no portfolio
  }
}

Portfolio *-- "many" BalanceChange
BalanceChangeReceipt ..> BalanceChange : copied from
LockedPortfolio ..> Portfolio : names

InsufficientFundsError -[hidden]down- Balance

note bottom of BalanceChange
  Amounts have up to 12 digits before the point and 4 after.
  Nothing here checks that cash_balance is the sum of its
  portfolio's changes. change_balance keeps that true.
  The foreign key to users is the string "users.user_id",
  so wallet never imports users' models.py.
end note

legend right
  <color:#0F6E56>■</color> Public: what other modules may import
  <color:#185FA5>■</color> Data: a read-only record, or a table
  <color:#A32D2D>■</color> Error: a DomainError
  + anyone holding one may use it
  A filled diamond means "owns": deleting
  a portfolio deletes its changes.
endlegend
@enduml
